From d122d975d9ea07d9a8c03ff988de85b6ef4afa50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:57:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: carry approval stops in creation provenance;
 bind delivery claims to exact operator receipts

Consent: a typed human timeout/deny at the approval boundary on a direct
`hermes kanban comment <t_id>` command is recorded in state.db and stamped
onto every card the session (or its descendant cards) creates as
created.consent_stops. Supervisor submission and the home executor refuse
an operator comment on a stopped target (consent_stop), across hosts.
Technical outcomes never stop or grant; an ordinary next user turn never
clears a stop; only an explicit same-session same-target approval
supersedes it for later cards. Created snapshots stay immutable.

Delivery: the operator result event carries operator_delivery (exact
request, target, caller run, executor, comment id and full SHA-256 of the
read-back body). The existing completion receipt accepts it as evidence
and complete_task verifies it against the Board's canonical request and
result rows; a summary that claims delivery to a target this card filed
an operator comment for, or to a replica-only foreign card, needs that
receipt. Pending/failed/unrelated/wrong actor/target/digest never prove
delivery. Transport (home execution, caller poll) uses the same canonical
decoder.

Task t_01a1d1d7998cda2a.
